# --- Databricks CLI sync state ----------------------------------------------
# `databricks sync` writes these next to a synced directory. Local build state,
# not source: it records absolute workspace paths including the owner's email,
# is regenerated on every sync, and would produce spurious diffs for anyone
# deploying from their own workspace.
.databricks/

# --- Generated app payload: DELIBERATELY NOT IGNORED -------------------------
# scripts/build_app.sh copies f1lake/ into each app directory, because a
# Databricks App deploys from a single source path and a sibling package is not
# importable at runtime.
#
# These copies were ignored at first, to avoid two files drifting apart. That
# was wrong: `databricks sync` honours .gitignore, so ignoring them silently
# stripped f1lake/ out of the deployment and the app failed on
# `from f1lake import schema` before serving a request. There is no way to have
# the payload deployed but untracked.
#
# So the copies are committed, and build_app.sh regenerates them. Run it before
# committing: `git diff` then shows any drift instead of hiding it.

# --- Warehouse query cache --------------------------------------------------
# Gold marts pulled from Delta by f1lake/seed_gold.py, cached so a failed seed
# does not re-spend a warehouse query. Derived data - Delta is the source of
# truth - and 1.8 MB of it. Regenerate with `seed_gold.py --refresh`.
data/f1_driver_performance.json
data/f1_championship.json

# Lap times: ~1,133 rows per race across 59 races. Large, slow to fetch, and
# fully regenerable with `python -m harvest.run_laps`. Pit stops ARE committed -
# they are small and are what the stint reconstruction depends on.
data/laps/

